      "text": "To find the value of \\( b \\) such that the equations \\( 2x + 7 = 3 \\) and \\( bx - 10 = -2 \\) have the same solution for \\( x \\), we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Solve the first equation \\( 2x + 7 = 3 \\) for \\( x \\).\n2. Substitute the solution of \\( x \\) into the second equation \\( bx - 10 = -2 \\) and solve for \\( b \\).\n\nLet's start with the first equation:\n\n\\[ 2x + 7 = 3 \\]\n\nSubtract 7 from both sides:\n\n\\[ 2x = 3 - 7 \\]\n\\[ 2x = -4 \\]\n\nDivide both sides by 2:\n\n\\[ x = \\frac{-4}{2} \\]\n\\[ x = -2 \\]\n\nNow that we have \\( x = -2 \\), we substitute this value into the second equation \\( bx - 10 = -2 \\):\n\n\\[ b(-2) - 10 = -2 \\]\n\nSimplify the left side:\n\n\\[ -2b - 10 = -2 \\]\n\nAdd 10 to both sides:\n\n\\[ -2b = -2 + 10 \\]\n\\[ -2b = 8 \\]\n\nDivide both sides by -2:\n\n\\[ b = \\frac{8}{-2} \\]\n\\[ b = -4 \\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\( b \\) is \\(\\boxed{-4}\\).",
