    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "Given the equations $2x+7=3$ and $bx-10=-2$, we need to find the value of $b$ such that both equations have the same solution $x$.\n\n### Step 1: Solve the first equation for $x$\nStarting with the equation:\n\\[ 2x + 7 = 3 \\]\nSubtract 7 from both sides:\n\\[ 2x = 3 - 7 \\]\n\\[ 2x = -4 \\]\nDivide both sides by 2:\n\\[ x = -2 \\]\n\n### Step 2: Substitute $x = -2$ into the second equation\nThe second equation is:\n\\[ bx - 10 = -2 \\]\nSubstitute $x = -2$ into this equation:\n\\[ b(-2) - 10 = -2 \\]\nSimplify the equation:\n\\[ -2b - 10 = -2 \\]\nAdd 10 to both sides:\n\\[ -2b = -2 + 10 \\]\n\\[ -2b = 8 \\]\nDivide both sides by -2:\n\\[ b = \\frac{8}{-2} \\]\n\\[ b = -4 \\]\n\n### Conclusion\nThe value of $b$ that makes both equations have the same solution $x$ is:\n\\[ \\boxed{-4} \\]",
