      "text": "Let's solve the given problem step by step.\n\nWe are given two equations:\n1. \\(2x + 7 = 3\\)\n2. \\(bx - 10 = -2\\)\n\nFirst, we solve the equation \\(2x + 7 = 3\\) for \\(x\\):\n\n\\[\n2x + 7 = 3\n\\]\n\nSubtract 7 from both sides:\n\n\\[\n2x = 3 - 7\n\\]\n\n\\[\n2x = -4\n\\]\n\nDivide both sides by 2:\n\n\\[\nx = \\frac{-4}{2}\n\\]\n\n\\[\nx = -2\n\\]\n\nSo, the solution to the first equation is \\(x = -2\\).\n\nNext, we substitute \\(x = -2\\) into the second equation \\(bx - 10 = -2\\) and solve for \\(b\\):\n\n\\[\nb(-2) - 10 = -2\n\\]\n\nDistribute \\(b\\):\n\n\\[\n-2b - 10 = -2\n\\]\n\nAdd 10 to both sides:\n\n\\[\n-2b = -2 + 10\n\\]\n\n\\[\n-2b = 8\n\\]\n\nDivide both sides by -2:\n\n\\[\nb = \\frac{8}{-2}\n\\]\n\n\\[\nb = -4\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of \\(b\\) is \\(\\boxed{-4}\\).",
